# {*} arg expansion (R7) — terminal opcode is invokeExpanded.
# Walker captures the command-name literal from the first push after
# expandStart. Bracket-substituted args (`puts {*}[list a b]`) are a
# sub-table B inlining case: Tcl 8.6 constant-folds the literal list
# and the resulting bytecode is split across "Command N:" headers in a
# way the per-command walker cannot resolve cleanly. The P1.2 bridge
# refines via cross-pc attribution; P1.1 covers the literal/var forms.
set args {a b}
foo {*}$args
set xs {c d e}
puts {*}$xs
---
  expand_args       cmd=2 name=foo
  expand_args       cmd=4 name=puts
